project:
  name: ai-cad-analyzer
  language: python
  description: >
    A full-stack application with a Streamlit frontend and a Django backend for analyzing 
    2D CAD PDF drawings using AI. The app extracts part-contact data via a Google Gemini model, 
    orchestrated through an n8n workflow. Outputs are provided as structured CSV or reports.

rules:
  - description: >
      The frontend is built with Streamlit. Users upload 2D CAD PDF drawings via Streamlit, 
      which interfaces with a Django REST API.
  - description: >
      Django handles user authentication, upload logging, file storage, and metadata management. 
      It forwards the uploaded files and metadata to the n8n webhook endpoint.
  - description: >
      n8n is configured to receive HTTP POST requests. It triggers a Google Gemini model call 
      to analyze the drawing and extract dimensions, tolerance data, and part relationships.
  - description: >
      Include prompt-tuning logic in the n8n node before calling Gemini, to improve result accuracy 
      on complex engineering drawings.
  - description: >
      n8n responds with a downloadable CSV file or a link to a report, which Django stores and 
      Streamlit presents to the user.
  - description: >
      Use Django REST Framework for building the API endpoints and Celery for managing asynchronous 
      processing if needed in future versions.
  - description: >
      The backend uses PostgreSQL as the primary database, configured via Django's settings.
      It stores user data, file uploads, metadata, and links to processed results.
  - description: >
      Django is integrated with Microsoft Azure Active Directory. All users log in using 
      their company Microsoft credentials via OAuth2 (Azure AD SSO).

